{"aggregate_id": "01KTYQQSAJA888YXKYBX24W2AJ", "aggregate_type": "Mission", "event_id": "01KTYQQSH46JK8JM3M8YNX0EXG", "event_type": "MissionCreated", "payload": {"created_at": "2026-06-12T20:17:54.006599+00:00", "friendly_name": "Pull-Based Deploy Pipeline with Tier Guard and Doctrinal Anchor", "mission_id": "01KTYQQSAJA888YXKYBX24W2AJ", "mission_number": null, "mission_slug": "pull-based-deploy-pipeline-01KTYQQS", "mission_type": "software-dev", "purpose_context": "Every mission that touches office2 today builds a one-shot deploy wrapper, reinventing patterns and occasionally reintroducing bug classes the governance prohibits (closed #162 conflated system crontab with openclaw-managed crons). This mission delivers a manifest-driven pull-based pipeline where office2 reads a deploys/queued/ directory every 5 minutes, runs a vetted Python library of primitives, enforces tier-aware controls in CI and at execute time, and anchors the discipline in CLAUDE.md, the project charter, issue templates, and the architecture signal-to-doc map. The result is that any future agent writing a spec for new work automatically incorporates the deploy story without operator prompting. Existing deploy scripts are grandfathered; sibling issue #548 handles their cleanup post-merge.", "purpose_tldr": "Replace ad-hoc deploy wrappers with a manifest-driven pull-based pipeline; anchor the deploy discipline in agent-facing docs so future specify/plan runs include it automatically.", "target_branch": "main", "wp_count": 0}, "project_slug": "kg-automation", "project_uuid": "2c011d09-8272-470c-b9e2-e9ccf8ad3fbd", "schema_version": "5.0.0", "timestamp": "2026-06-12T20:17:54.212987+00:00"}
